(Purpose and usage:) Tj T*
(KinetiQ BLE Diag is an academic Bluetooth/wearables diagnostic application) Tj T*
(developed as university coursework \(KinetiQ project\). Within the Wear) Tj T*
(Engine scope, it calls DeviceClient.getBondedDevices\(\) to obtain the list) Tj T*
(of the user's paired Huawei wearable devices \(device identifiers, model,) Tj T*
(connection status\), so that the user can explicitly select the device) Tj T*
(whose diagnostics are being performed. It may optionally subscribe to the) Tj T*
(device connection status through MonitorClient while the app screen is) Tj T*
(open.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(All processing is performed on the device and is read-only. The app does) Tj T*
(not read, store or transmit any health metrics through Wear Engine, does) Tj T*
(not modify device settings, and does not send files to the device. The) Tj T*
(Huawei Health app hosts the communication channel; this app only displays) Tj T*
(diagnostic results locally on its own screen. No data is shared with any) Tj T*
(third party or server.) Tj T*
ET
